## TASK
################################################################################

You will be given two sketches:
- A mobile sketch showing the intended layout at narrow viewport width
- A desktop sketch showing the intended layout at wide viewport width

Wireframe Interpretation Guide
Use the following standardized meanings when reading the sketches:

Rectangle with an "X": Image, banner, hero image, or thumbnail
Thick straight or wavy line(s): Heading or title text
Wavy horizontal lines: Paragraph text or body content
Box: Button
Box with wavy line inside: Text input or form field
Plain rectangular bar (no waves): Navigation bar, container, or section block separator
Hamburger icon (three stacked lines): Collapsed mobile navigation

Generate a single, complete, self-contained HTML file that implements the page
shown in the sketches. All CSS must be inside a <style> tag in the <head>. All
JavaScript must be inside a <script> tag at the end of the <body>. No external
files, no CDN imports, no frameworks. One file only.

